 "error": null,
 "final_text": "I have successfully identified and fixed the root cause of the bias in Quasi-Monte Carlo pricing of path-dependent products when using Sobol sampling with Brownian bridge.\n\n## Problem Analysis\nThe issue was in both the CPU simulation engine (`simulation_engine.hpp`) and the AAD simulation engine (`simulation_engine_aad.hpp`). When using `mc_sampler = SamplerKind::Sobol` with `mc_brownian_bridge = true`, the code was incorrectly using the full simulation dimension (`dim`) for both:\n1. Creating the Sobol sequence \n2. Allocating the point vector\n3. Calling `next_gaussian()` \n\nHowever, the `BridgedGaussians::map()` function expects the point to be structured with only `n * factors` coordinates (where `n` is the number of time steps and `factors` is the number of Brownian factors) for the bridge part, not the full simulation dimension.\n\n## Solution Implemented\nI modified both files to:\n1. **For CPU simulation engine** (`simulation_engine.hpp`):\n   - Allocate `point` vector with size `bridge->n_ * bridge->factors_` instead of `dim`\n   - Create `SobolSequence` with dimension `bridge->n_ * bridge->factors_` instead of `dim`\n   - Call `sobol.next_gaussian()` with the correct dimension\n\n2. **For AAD simulation engine** (`simulation_engine_aad.hpp`):\n   - Resize `point` vector with size `bridge->n_ * bridge->factors_` instead of `dim`\n   - Create `SobolSequence` with dimension `bridge->n_ * bridge->factors_` instead of `dim`\n   - Call `sobol.next_gaussian()` with the correct dimension\n\n## Key Changes\n- **File 1**: `/workspace/project/include/quantModeling/engines/mc/simulation_engine.hpp`\n- **File 2**: `/workspace/project/include/quantModeling/engines/mc/simulation_engine_aad.hpp`\n\nThe fix is minimal, maintains the same public API, and ensures that Sobol sequences are generated with the correct dimensions that match the expectations of the Brownian bridge mapping functions, eliminating the bias in path-dependent product pricing.",
